# Thumbnail and title rules (25 Sep 2026)

Readable copy with the evidence: `00_Brand/Channel-Setup/THUMBNAIL_AND_TITLE_RULES.md`.

## Titles

- A familiar noun in the first four words (your hands, your bones, a table, a drop of water, you).
- One concrete promise: a familiar thing turned strange; the body or the everyday seen for the first time; a yes/no about what everyone believed; a prediction that came true; one real number or object; an accident that changed everything.
- Longs: the searched phrase, subject in the first five words, the thing over the method. Not *How Did We Discover X?* every week.
- **FAIL:** abstract labels or riddles (*What other table has empty chairs?* 4 views), hedged claims, hashtags, series suffixes, a copy of a live title, fear framing. Under about 60 characters.

## Long thumbs (the live look, 30 Sep 2026)

- **Painted 3D cartoon key art**, full bleed, warm library/lab light. Never flat graphics, split panels or a plain dark background. Reference: `02_…002…/08_Thumbnail/LIVE_THUMB_LOCK.md`.
- **One giant hero object, ~2/3 of the frame, right.** The Explorer **small, lower left**, on model, looking at it.
- **Painted lettering left:** cream words + one gold punch word, serif display, small gold flourishes, same on every thumb. 2–5 words readable at 168×94: `python3 00_Brand/Channel-Setup/tools/thumb_preview.py long <thumb> --out <sheet>`.
- Main thumb may paint the title in; the other variants use 2–3 hook words that add to it.
- No AI-made text or numbers except the lettering; any symbol or number checked and fixed by hand. Nothing in the bottom-right corner; every object fully in frame.
- Make with an image model using a live thumb + the Explorer reference as references. Test & Compare with 3; judge CTR past about 500 impressions.

## Shorts

- **Frame 0 is the thumbnail in the feed:** the named thing, moving. Never the Explorer, a blank card grid or a dark card.
- Frame-0 caption: the promise in 2–4 words, cap height about 8–10%, yellow hook word.
- Custom cover: the title's hook words, 2–4 words, at least 60% of frame width, vertically centred. Check with `thumb_preview.py short`.
- **Two lettering styles (30 Sep 2026):** long thumbs = serif, cream + one gold punch word, flourishes. Shorts covers = chunky rounded gold/cream, thick outline, one small teal middle word, on a painted 3D scene with the Explorer as a small reaction. Never mix them; never a film-frame crop with a text box. Compare each new one on a sheet with live ones of the same format: `python3 00_Brand/Channel-Setup/tools/style_sheet.py long|short <new> --out <sheet>`.
